The graph shows part of a boat's journey. Find:
(a) its acceleration from $2$ to $8$ s;
(b) the magnitude of its deceleration from $8$ to $12$ s.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=3mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,very thin,xstep=10mm,ystep=6mm] (0,0) grid (12,12);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(13,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,13);
\foreach \t in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12} {\draw[black] (\t,0)--(\t,-0.25);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,-0.25) {$\t$};}
\foreach \v in {2,4,6,8,10,12} {\draw[black] (0,\v)--(-0.15,\v);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.15,\v) {$\v$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-2.2,6) {Speed (m/s)};
\node at (6,-3) {Time (s)};
\draw[graphblue,thick] (2,3)--(8,12)--(12,4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Subtract both the starting speed and the starting time.

$\begin{aligned}\text{Acceleration}&=\frac{12-3}{8-2}\\&=\frac{9}{6}\\&=1.5\text{ m/s}^2\end{aligned}$

(b) The speed decreases by $8$ m/s over $4$ s.

$\begin{aligned}\text{Acceleration}&=\frac{4-12}{12-8}\\&=-2\text{ m/s}^2\end{aligned}$
The deceleration magnitude is $2$ m/s².

The dashed steps show the speed changes and time intervals.

[tikz]
